formation Library of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism",item4:"(",item5:" or URL of the relevant Website)",item6:"[Example of additional description in cases of using Content by editing/processing, etc.]",item7:'Created by XX Co., Ltd. based on "name of Content" (Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism) or otherwise'}},subsection2:{title:"(2)“This Content” where “This Terms of Use” does not apply",contents1:{item1:"The following contents are the responsibility of the user to follow the rules set forth in the following paragraphs.",item2:"1. For Content to which a state has rights and the rules for the use thereof, refer to the following information:",item3:"(i) Digital National Land Information (Digital National Land Information download site)",item4:'(ii) GSI Tiles "Shaded-relief map" (Geospatial Information Authority of Japan)',item5:"(iii) Hazard Map Portal Site",item6:"(iv) City Planning Decision GIS Data National Data (City Planning Decision GIS Data National Data download page)",item7:"(v) Data Grid Square Statistic (Statistical Geographic Information System)",item8:"(vi) Liquefaction tendency map based on topographic classification (City Bureau, Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism)"},contents2:{item1:"2. The map used on the screen displaying a map shall be used in accordance with the following terms of use:",item2:"(i) ZENRIN CO., LTD. ZENRIN Maps API",item3:"(ii) GSI Tiles (Geospatial Information Authority of Japan)"}}},articles:{article0:{title:"Terms of Use"},article1:{title:"Article 1 Purpose and Application",contents:{content1:"(1) These Terms of Use set forth the terms of use of this Website.",content2:"(2) The user is asked to be sure to read carefully these Terms of Use before starting to use this Website. Only those who consent to these Terms of Use may use this Website.",content3:"(3) By the use of this Website, the user shall be deemed by the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism to have consented to these Terms of Use.",content4:"(4) Official versions of these Terms of Use and of the explanation on this Website given by the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism (including those in this Website) shall be in the Japanese language only and shall not be in any other languages. If there is any discrepancy between the Japanese language version and those in any other language, the Japanese language version shall prevail and those in other languages cannot supplement or modify the Japanese language version. Inquiries, etc. on the usage shall be made in Japanese."}},article2:{title:"Article 2 Definitions",contents:{detail:"The terms used in these Terms of Use shall be defined as follows.",content1:'(1)	"Land Price Publication" shall mean the publication under Article 2 Paragraph 1 of the Public Notice of Land Prices Act (Act No. 49 of 1969) which publishes the normal price per 1 m2 as of January 1 of each year of a standard point of land (standard lot) selected by the Land Appraisal Committee of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism based on the appraisal of two (2) licensed real estate appraisers (real estate appraiser).',content2:'(2)	"Appraisal Report Information" shall mean the information of the appraisal report prepared by the licensed real estate appraiser in determining the price for Land Price Publication.',content3:'(3) "Land Price Research by Prefectural Government" shall mean the determination and announcement of the standard price of a benchmark lot as of July 1 of each year by the prefectural governor conducted for the purpose of having such price serve as the standard for price review, etc. in cases of restriction on land transaction by the prefectural government or calculation of purchase price by a local government, etc. or for other purposes under Article 9 of the Order for Enforcement of the National Land Use Planning Act (Cabinet Order No. 387 of 1974).',content4:'(4) "Real Estate Transaction Price Information" shall mean the real estate transaction price information held and provided by the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism that consist of data obtained by collecting answers to questionnaires regarding transactions of lands/buildings and processed so as to make individual properties unidentifiable.',content5:'(5) "Contract price information" shall mean the real estate transaction price information stored in the computer network system (REINS) operated by the real estate distribution organizations designated by the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism, which is made available to the public by the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism, a real estate transaction information service for consumers, after being processed so as to make individual transactions unidentifiable.',content6:'(6) "Download service" shall mean the service to provide real estate transaction price information, contract price information, and appraisal report information held by the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism on the Internet through this Website.'}},article3:{title:"Article 3 Notes for Use of Website",contents:{content1:{item:"(1) Due to the difference in the accuracy of information and creation/update time, etc. of the information, there may be some deviations among overlaid Content or between the Content and the background map image."},content2:{item:"(2) Some Content does not cover entire regions due to reasons such as not being able to obtain permission for use from the source."},content3:{item:"(3) Due to the difference in the creation/update time of each Content, some data may not be the latest information."},content4:{item:"(4) Content is expected to be used as reference information but not as information guaranteed for the use in the explanation of important matters or procedures such as application for building certification in real estate transactions."},content5:{item1:"(5) The API Functions provided on this Website shall be used in accordance with the following ",item2:"terms of use",item3:"."},content6:{item:"(6) The user shall be liable for any damage suffered by the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism as a result of the user's use of the Content beyond the permitted scope or as a result of infringing any right to the Content.'"},content7:{item:'(7) The user shall not use the title "Real Estate Information Library" for products, services, applications, etc. unless there is a permission by the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism. When using the name of "Real Estate Information Library", please contact the inquiry form.'}}},article4:{title:"Article 4 Notes for Use of Information on Published Land Price and Standard Price of Benchmark Lot Determined by Land Price Research by Prefectural Government",contents:{content1:{item:'(1) Either published land price or standard price of a benchmark lot determined by Land Price Research by Prefectural Government (hereinafter referred to as "Published Land Price, etc.") indicates a price (normal price) that is considered to be established in a transaction without special circumstances such as hasty selling or aggressive buying on either of the seller or the buyer, as determined by the appraisal method based on the Ministerial Ordinance on Standards for Appraisal of Standard Lot and the Real Property Appraisal Standards, etc.'},content2:{item1:"(2) Published Land Price, etc. indicates a standard lot price of the neighboring area.",item2:'(i) For either the standard lot for the Land Price Publication or benchmark lot for land price research (hereinafter referred to as "Standard Lot, etc."), a standard piece of lot in terms of the status of land use, environment, acreage and shape etc. in the neighboring area (a group of neighboring lands including the Standard Lot, etc. whose purpose of use is considered to be the same as such Standard Lot, etc. such as residential land or commercial land; hereinafter the same shall apply) has been selected. ',item3:"(ii)	Therefore, the Published Land Price, etc. indicates the standard level of lot price in the neighboring area but not the highest or lowest land price."},content3:{item1:"(3)	Published Land Price, etc. does not uniformly indicate the price of the entire land in the neighboring area.",item2:"(i)	Land price varies depending on the factors constituting the individual price such as acreage, shape and conditions of adjacent roads even located in the same neighboring area as well as in different areas.",item3:"(ii)	Published Land Price, etc. is also the price of a specific lot with specific conditions such as acreage, shape and conditions of adjacent roads. Therefore, when calculating a price that is balanced with the Published Land Price, etc., it is necessary to compare the factors that constitute the individual prices of Standard Lot, etc. and those of the land, even if the land is located in a neighboring area of the Standard Lot, etc.",item4:"(iii)	Based on the above items, it is necessary to fully compare the factors of circumstances published with the prices when using Published Land Price, etc. in connection with an actual land transaction when calculating a price."},content4:{item:"(4)	Published Land Price, etc. indicates a price per 1 m2 as of the base date of Standard Lot, etc. (Land Price Publication: January 1; Land Price Research by Prefectural Government: July 1) (however, the price of forest land is indicated as the price per 0.1 ha in the Land Price Research by Prefectural Government). Generally, the price of land varies depending on the time of transaction. Since the Published Land Prices, etc. are the prices determined as of January 1 or July 1 as the base date, it is necessary to calculate the prices by taking into account fluctuations in the price of land due to difference in the valuation date, when using the Published Land Prices, etc."},content5:{item:"(5)	For Land Price Research by Prefectural Government, see also the official information of the prefectural government and Website of the relevant prefecture."}}},article5:{title:"Article 5 Notes for Use of Real Estate Transaction Price Information and Contract Price Information",contents:{content1:{item:"(1) As all lands/buildings have their unique attributes (including location, road access, area, and purpose of use, etc.), their transactions reflect the unique attributes of the relevant land/building. In addition, the actual transaction price may vary from the price expected in normal transactions reflecting various circumstances on the part of the buyer or seller (including hasty selling or hasty buying)."},content2:{item:'(2) Both real estate transaction price information and contract price information (hereinafter referred to as "Real Estate Transaction Price Information, etc.") may contain information on the same transaction.'},content3:{item:"(3) Real Estate Transaction Price Information, etc., data are added every quarter term. However, the user is hereby cautioned that real estate transaction price information may be added from time to time after the publication."}}},article6:{title:"Article 6 Prohibited Matters",contents:{content1:{item1:"(1)Users of the Website shall be prohibited from engaging in any of the following acts when using the Website.",item2:"(i)An act that is contrary to law or public policy",item3:"(ⅱ)Acts of illegally accessing or attempting to access the Website, its servers, networks or other systems",item4:"(ⅲ)Acts that violate copyrights, trademark rights, or other intellectual property rights contained in the Website",item5:"(ⅳ)Damaging the credibility of the Website or interfering with the operation of the Website by spreading rumors or using fraudulent means or force",item6:"(ⅴ)Destruction or interference of the functions of the servers or networks of the Website or any other act having an adverse effect on the Website",item7:"(ⅵ)Analysis, falsification, duplication, or secondary use of systems, software, protocols, etc. related to the Website through reverse engineering, etc.",item8:"(ⅶ)Conduct that interferes with or is likely to interfere with the operation of the Website"},content2:{item:"(2)The Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism may suspend the use of the Website without prior notice if any of the Users of the Website has committed or is likely to commit any of the acts listed in the items of the preceding paragraph."}}},article7:{title:"Article 7 Linking to the Website",contents:{content1:{item1:"(1)	Linking to this Website is permitted. When linking, however, the user shall make sure to link to the ",item2:"home page",item3:"."},content2:{item:'(2)	When linking to this Website, the user shall expressly indicate that the link is to the "Real Estate Information Library of Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism".'},content3:{item:"(3)	When setting a link to this Website, the user shall pay attention to the layout and expression, etc. so as not to cause the visitor to wrongly think that the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism is co-hosting, participating, backing, sponsoring or supervising or otherwise involved."},content4:{item:"(4) When using a bookmark, the user shall use the URL specified in Paragraph 1 to help the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism keep track of visits and use of this Website."}}},article8:{title:"Article 8 Revision of Terms",contents:{content1:{item:"(1) These Terms of Use may be modified without prior notice."},content2:{item:"(2) On and after the effective date of the revised Terms of Use, the revised Terms of Use shall apply to the use of this Website."},content3:{item:"(3) The Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism shall announce the revision of these Terms of Use on the Website of the Real Estate Information Library; provided, however, that the revision may be announced by other means if the announcement on the Website of the Real Estate Information Library is difficult."},content4:{item:"(4) By the use of this Website after the announcement under the preceding paragraph, the user shall be deemed by the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism to have consented to the application of the revised Terms of Use."}}},article9:{title:"Article 9 Other",contents:{content1:{item:"(1)	Content may be modified, moved or deleted, etc. without prior notice."},content2:{item:"(2) The Website may be changed, moved, or deleted or the services of the Website may be suspended, discontinued, or abolished without prior notice."},content3:{item:"(3) The Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism may abolish all or part of this Website due to unavoidable circumstances."},content4:{item1:'(4) The Privacy Policy regarding the use of this Website shall be as set forth in the following Website as well as in these Terms of Use and "Real Estate Information Library API Terms of Use":',item2:"Privacy Policy of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism"},content5:{item1:"(5) Linking, copyright, and disclaimer related to this Website shall be as set forth in the following Website as well as in these Terms of Use:",item2:'"About the Copyright" in the Website of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism.'},content6:{item:"(6) These Terms of Use are established as of April 1, 2024.(Revised on June 18, 2025.) "},content7:{item1:"(7) It is recommended to view this Website using the following devices, OS, and web browsers. Web browsers should be the latest versions.",item2:"[PC]",item3:"-	Windows×Google Chrome",item4:"-	Windows×Microsoft Edge（* Internet Explorer Mode is not supported）.",item5:"* Recommended OS version: Windows 10, Windows 11",item6:"[Tablet/Smartphone]",item7:"-	iOS×Safari",item8:"-	iOS×Google Chrome",item9:"-	Android×Google Chrome",item10:"* Recommended OS version: iOS16 or later, Android 10 or later"}}}}},section2:{title:"API Terms of Use of Real Estate Information Library",articles:{article1:{title:"Article 1	Purpose and Application",contents:{content1:{item:'(1) These Terms of Use set forth the terms of use of the API functions (hereinafter referred to as the "API Functions") provided by the Real Estate Information Library with the "Terms of Use of the Real Estate Information Library."'},content2:{item:'(2) Any matter not covered by these Terms of Use shall be subject to the "Terms of Use of the Real Estate Information Library." In such case, the terms "Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism","Content" and "user" shall be read as "Provider","Provided Information" and "API User",respectively.'},content3:{item:'(3) The API User may use the "API Functions" without cost. Provided Information may be used freely without cost. However, any cost for the use of the API Functions such as communication expenses shall be borne by the API User.'},content4:{item:"(4) Official versions of these Terms of Use and of the explanation on the API Functions given by the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism (including those in this Website) shall be in the Japanese language only and shall not be in any other languages."},content5:{item:"If there is any discrepancy between the Japanese language version and those in any other language, the Japanese language version shall prevail and those in other languages cannot supplement or modify the Japanese language version. "},content6:{item:"Inquiries, etc. on the usage shall be made in Japanese."}}},article2:{title:"Article 2	Definitions",contents:{content:"　The terms used in these Terms of Use shall be defined as follows.",items:{item1:"(i) Operating Administrator: the person who operates and administers the Real Estate Information Library including the API Functions, which is the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism.",item2:"(ii)	Contract Operator: the person who contracted all or part of the operations necessary for the provision of the API Functions from the Operating Administrator.",item3:"(iii) Provider: Operating Administrator and Contract Operator.",item4:"(iv)	API User: the person (including state and local government) who consents to these Terms of Use and uses the API Functions. The API User does not include End Users.",item5:"(v) API Key: the identification code of the software that uses the API issued for the purpose of using the API Functions.",item6:"(vi)	Application: an application or program, etc. developed by the API User incorporating the API Functions.",item7:"(vii) Provided Information: information provided to an Application through the API Functions.",item8:"(viii) End User: a user who uses an Application.",item9:"(ix)	Antisocial Forces: an organized crime group, a company associated with an organized crime group, a corporate racketeer or a person similar to the foregoing, or a member thereof, including a person whose officer (i.e., employee executing the business, director or executive officer, or a person similar to the foregoing) is an Antisocial Force."}}},article3:{title:"Article 3	Application for Use",contents:{content1:{item1:"　A person who intends to use the API Functions shall declare to the Provider that, at the time of the application and for the future, he/she does not fall under an Antisocial Force nor does he/she allow Antisocial Forces to use his/her name, and apply for ",item2:"use of the API by entering necessary information through the application page",item3:".",item4:"　If, after submitting the application, there is any change in the information registered at the time of the application such as contact information, the details of the change shall be promptly notified to the Provider using the ",item5:"inquiry form",item6:", unless the application has been rejected."}}},article4:{title:"Article 4	Consent to Terms",contents:{content:"　A person who intends to use the API Functions shall carefully read these Terms of Use before using the API Functions and submit an application for use of the API Functions after consenting to these Terms of Use."}},article5:{title:"Article 5	User Agreement",contents:{content1:{content:"(1)	The Provider shall review the application for use of the API submitted under Article 3. The Provider may refuse the application if any of the following items applies:",items:{item1:"(i)	The Provider determines that the applicant is likely to fail to perform his/her contractual obligations if the applicant enters into a user agreement with the Provider based on the applicant's past failure to perform his/her contractual obligations with the Provider or for other reasons;",item2:"(ii)	The Provider determines that there is a false statement in the application;",item3:"(iii)	The Provider determines that there is a significant operational or technical difficulty in providing the API Functions to the applicant;",item4:"(iv)	The Provider determines that the applicant is likely to use the API Functions in a manner that could harm the reputation of the Provider;",item5:"(v)	The Provider determines that the applicant is an Antisocial Force; or",item6:"(vi)	The Provider otherwise determines that it is inappropriate to accept the application."}},content2:{item1:"(2)	When the Provider accepts the application after the review under the preceding paragraph, it shall issue an API Key and notify the API User of such API Key by email. When the notice reaches to the API User, a user agreement with the content of these Terms of Use shall be formed between the applicant and the Provider.",item2:"　If the applicant has submitted an application on behalf of the organization to which the applicant belongs (a business operator or a department or division, etc. belonging to the business operator), the unit of the organization shall be authorized for the use, and the API Key shall be notified to the applicant who submitted the application on behalf of the organization."},content3:{item1:"(3) When any of the following items applies, the API User shall promptly notify the Provider using the ",item2:"inquiry form",item3:".",item4:"(i) The API Key turns out to have been illegally used by a third party (any person other than the API User or Provider) or is suspected to have been illegally used;",item5:"(ii)	The API Key was lost;",item6:"(iii) Use of the API Key is suspended, discontinued, or abolished."},content4:{item:"(4) When the Provider has received a notification under Item (i) of the preceding paragraph or when it determines that the API Key has been or is suspected to have been illegally used by a third party, it may immediately suspend the use of the API Functions."},content5:{item1:"(5)	If there is no record of the user's access to the API Functions using the API Key for a period starting on either of the following dates to the day on which three (3) years elapses, the Provider may suspend the use of the API Functions:",item2:"(i)	The last day on which the API Functions were accessed; or",item3:"(ii)	The day on which the API Key was issued, if Item (i) does not apply."},content6:{item:"(6) If a notice does not reach to the address registered by the API User or is rejected or returned, the Provider may suspend the use of the API Functions."},content7:{item:"(7) If the application for the service is rejected by the Provider under the provision of Paragraph 1, the Provider shall promptly notify the applicant to that effect. The Provider has no obligation to disclose the reason of the rejection."}}},article6:{title:"Article 6	Provision of Information on Status of Use",contents:{content1:"(1)	The Provider may ask the user about the status of use of the API Functions and the usage needs of the Content, etc. provided on the Website by way of questionnaires, email or other means. In such cases, the user shall provide the information to the extent that he/she may disclose it.",content2:"(2)	The Provider may disclose the information provided under the preceding paragraph as an example of use."}},article7:{title:"Article 7	Credit Display",contents:{content1:"　When providing services using the API Functions, the following credit shall be displayed. The place to display the credit is not designated so long as the users are able to see.",content2:'　"This service uses the API Functions of the Real Estate Information Library of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism, but does not guarantee the up-to-dateness, accuracy or completeness, etc. of the Provided Information."'}},article8:{title:"Article 8	Obligations/Responsibilities of the API User",contents:{content1:"(1)	The API User shall clearly indicate to the End User that Applications have been developed and operated by the API User at his/her responsibility. In doing so, the API User shall clearly indicate the scope of responsibilities of the API User and of the End User appropriately in a manner that the End User can understand.",content2:"(2)	The API User shall appropriately manage the API Key issued to him/her at his/her responsibility and discretion and shall not disclose it to any third party.",content3:'(3) When the API User provides an Application and related services (hereinafter referred to as the "Application, etc.") to an End User, he/she shall do so at his/her expense and responsibility.',content4:"(4) In providing an Application, etc. to an End User, the API User shall comply with the Act on the Protection of Personal Information, Act on Specified Commercial Transactions, Act against Unjustifiable Premiums and Misleading Representations, Consumer Contract Act and other laws and regulations.",content5:"(5) If an unauthorized access, etc. has occurred in connection with the use of the API Functions or provision of Application, etc., if leakage, divulgence, or falsification, etc., or disposal of properties caused by such unauthorized access, etc. has occurred, or if the API User has recognized the likelihood thereof, the API User shall immediately report to the Provider.",content6:"(6) When the provision of the preceding paragraph applies, the API User shall promptly take countermeasures and work with the Provider to investigate the cause and take countermeasures. In such case, the Provider may restrict or suspend the API User's use of the API Functions until sufficient countermeasures are taken.",content7:"(7)	In order to respond to occurrences of unauthorized access, etc., the API User shall record and store access logs necessary for the investigation of the cause, etc. of such potential unauthorized access, etc."}},article9:{title:"Article 9	Prohibited Acts",contents:{content1:{item:"(1) The API User shall not transfer his/her title under the user agreement to a third party, or assign, cause a third party to assume, or provide as collateral or otherwise divert all or part of the rights and obligations arising from the user agreement without the prior written consent of the Operating Administrator."},content2:{item1:"(2)	The API User may not commit the following acts in the use of the API Functions:",item2:"(i)	Use or try to use the API Functions for a purpose contrary to these Terms of Use;",item3:"(ii)	Engage in an act that threatens the safety of the nation’s citizens;",item4:"(iii)	Engage in an act that is contrary to law or public policy",item5:"(iv)	Engage in an act that interferes with or is likely to interfere with the operation of the API Functions or use thereof by a third party;",item6:"(v)	Engage in an act that causes or is likely to cause disadvantage or damage to the Provider or a third party; or",item7:"(vi)	Engage in either of the following acts in connection with the user agreement by himself/herself or using a third party:",item8:"1. Act of using threatening language or behavior or violence against the Operating Administrator; or",item9:"2. Act of obstructing the operations of the Operating Administrator or damaging the trust of the Operating Administrator by fraudulent means or force; or",item10:"(vii)	Create or operate an Application that contains any of the following items or to provide services related thereto:",item11:"1.	Content that violates these Terms of Use;",item12:"2.	Content that violates or is likely to violate laws and regulations or public order and morals;",item13:"3.	Content that infringes the property rights, intellectual property rights, credit, honor, privacy rights, image rights or other rights of the Provider, an End User or other third party; or",item14:"4.	Content that interferes with, destroys or restricts or is likely to interfere with, destroy or restrict the appropriate operation of software, hardware or communication devices, etc., such as computer viruses."},content3:{item:"(3)	If the API User has committed any of the acts set forth in the items of the preceding paragraph or there are reasonable grounds to suspect that the API User has committed such an act, or if the Provider determines that the use of the API Functions by the API User is inappropriate, the Provider may request the API User to correct the situation."},content4:{item:"(4) If the API User has committed any of the acts set forth in the items of Paragraph 2 or there are reasonable grounds to suspect that the API User has committed such an act, or if the Provider determines that the use of the API Functions by the API User is inappropriate, the Provider may request the API User to correct the situation."}}},article10:{title:"Article 10	Suspension of Use",contents:{content1:{item:"　The Provider may immediately suspend the use of the API Functions or immediately terminate the user agreement without prior notice if the API User has violated any of the provisions of these terms of the API and Terms of Use of Real Estate Information Library."}}},article11:{title:"Article 11	No Warranty and Disclaimer",contents:{content1:{item1:"The Provider makes no warranty regarding the API Functions including those on the matters set forth in the following items:",item2:"(1)	Defects or failures that the use of the API Functions may cause to the usage environment (limited to the scope affected by the use of API);",item3:"(2)	Accuracy, reliability, completeness, legality, non-infringement, validity and fitness for specific purpose of the API Functions or Provided Information;",item4:"(3)	Errors, bugs, trouble, interruption or other defects or security flaws in the system that provides the API Functions; or",item5:"(4)	Compliance with the laws and regulations, and internal rules, etc. of industry associations applicable to the API User."}}},article12:{title:"Article 12	Indemnity and Compensation",contents:{content1:{item:"　The purpose and method of use of the API Functions shall be at the discretion and responsibility of the API User and the Provider shall bear absolutely no responsibility. The API User shall be fully responsible for any damage (including, but not limited to, damages caused by any and all acts (including omission) conducted by a third party with the API Key issued under Article 5 Paragraph 2) suffered by the API User or a third party as a result of or in connection with the use of the API Functions regardless of reason and the Provider shall bear absolutely no responsibility."}}},article13:{title:"Article 13	Information Collection and Purpose of Use",contents:{content1:"(1)	For the issuance of the API Key referred to in Article 5, it is necessary to register a name, email address and purpose of use, etc. The API User may also be requested to register the organization to which he/she belongs and other necessary information. When a user under the age of 16 intends to register his/her user attributes, such user shall register with the consent of his/her parent or guardian.",content2:"(2)	Information collected under the preceding paragraph may be used for reference in future policy planning. The information may also be used to identify the computer of the API User and to distribute information by email (communication in the event of a failure or other communication on the operation, or inquiry about the usage status of the API Functions, etc.)."}},article14:{title:"Article 14	Revision of Terms",contents:{content1:"(1)	These Terms of Use may be revised without prior notice when the Provider considers it necessary.",content2:"(2)	After the effective date of the revised Terms of Use, the revised Terms of Use shall apply to the use of the API Functions.",content3:"(3)	The Provider shall announce the revision of these Terms of Use on the Website of the Real Estate Information Library; provided, however, that the revision may be announced by other means if the announcement on the Website of the Real Estate Information Library is difficult.",content4:"(4)	If the API User uses the available functions after the announcement under the preceding paragraph, he/she shall be deemed to have consented to the application of the revised Terms of Use."}},article15:{title:"Article 15	Termination of Provision",contents:{content1:"(1) The Provider may suspend, discontinue, or abolish the provision of the API Functions, and change, move, or delete the service to be provided without prior notice. If the provision of the API Functions is abolished, the user agreement shall automatically terminate concurrently with the abolition of the provision of the API Functions.",content2:"(2) The Provider shall announce the abolition of the API Functions on the Website of the Real Estate Information Library; provided, however, that the revision may be announced by other means if the announcement on the Website of the Real Estate Information Library is difficult.",content3:"(3) The Provider shall not be liable for any damage suffered by the API User due to the abolition of the provision of the API Functions under Paragraph 1."}},article16:{title:"Article 16	Entrustment of Service Operation",contents:{content:"　The Operating Administrator may entrust all or part of the operations necessary for the provision of the API Functions to a Contract Operator. In such cases, the Operating Administrator shall impose the same level of obligations as those of the Operating Administrator set forth in these Terms of Use on the Contract Operator."}},article17:{title:"Article 17	Governing Law and Jurisdiction",contents:{content:"　The user agreement shall be governed by the laws of Japan. The Provider and the API User agree that any and all the disputes arising from or in connection with the user agreement shall be subject to the exclusive agreed jurisdiction of the district court having jurisdiction over the location of the Operating Administrator (which is the Tokyo District Court, as of the date of establishment of these Terms of Use) for the first instance."}},supplementaryProvisions1:{title:"Supplementary Provisions",contents:{content:"　These Terms of Use shall take effect on April 1, 2024."}},supplementaryProvisions2:{title:"Supplementary Provisions",contents:{content:"　These revised Terms of Use shall take effect on August 28, 2024."}},supplementaryProvisions3:{title:"Supplementary Provisions",contents:{content:"　These revised Terms of Use shall take effect on October 30, 2024."}},supplementaryProvisions4:{title:"Supplementary Provisions",contents:{content:"　These revised Terms of Use shall take effect on June 18, 2025."}}}}},top:{breadcrumb:{top:"Top",help:"マニュアル・ヘルプ"},title:"マニュアル・ヘルプ",introduction:"「不動産情報 ライブラリ」のヘルプでは、概要、操作説明を通して、システムの利用方法を説明します。",tableOfContents:"目次",period:"・・・",mapManual:{name:"1. Webの利用方法（地図表示）",explain:"地図表示に関するWebの利用方法を説明します。"},realEstatePricesManual:{name:"2. Webの利用方法（不動産価格（取引価格・成約価格）情報）",explain:"不動産価格（取引価格・成約価格）情報に関するWebの利用方法を説明します。"},landPricesManual:{name:"3. Webの利用方法（地価公示・地価調査）",explain:"地価公示・地価調査に関するWebの利用方法を説明します。"},realEstatePricesAbout:{name:"4. 不動産価格（取引価格・成約価格）情報の制度と用語",explain:"不動産価格（取引価格・成約価格）情報の制度と用語を説明します。"},landPricesAbout:{name:"5. 地価公示・地価調査の制度と用語",explain:"地価公示・地価調査の制度と用語を説明します。"},realEstateAppraisalReport:{name:"6. 鑑定評価書の見方",